<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Present Perfect | B1 for Schools · Castle School</title>
<style>
:root{--navy:#073b82;--blue:#0755b8;--red:#df3028;--ink:#17243a;--muted:#63718a;--paper:#f5f7fb;--line:#dce4f0;--green:#168451;--amber:#a96800}
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;line-height:1.55}
.hero{background:linear-gradient(130deg,#062b61,#0755b8);color:white;padding:28px 18px 34px;text-align:center;position:relative;overflow:hidden}
.hero:after{content:"";position:absolute;width:300px;height:300px;border:1px solid #ffffff22;border-radius:50%;right:-90px;top:-180px;box-shadow:0 0 0 35px #ffffff0b,0 0 0 75px #ffffff08}
.logo{width:112px;height:112px;object-fit:contain;background:#fff;border-radius:22px;padding:7px;box-shadow:0 8px 24px #001a4433}
.brand{font-size:.76rem;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:800;margin:10px 0 3px;color:#dbeaff}
h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.35rem);line-height:1.08;margin:8px 0;font-weight:850;letter-spacing:-.04em}
.subtitle{margin:0;color:#e4efff;font-size:1.02rem}
.level{display:inline-block;margin-top:16px;border:1px solid #ffffff77;border-radius:99px;padding:5px 13px;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.08em}
main{max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 16px 60px}
.intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr;gap:16px;margin-bottom:18px}
.panel,.exercise{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;padding:21px;box-shadow:0 5px 18px #17345c08}
h2{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--navy);font-size:1.35rem;letter-spacing:-.02em}
h3{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:1.08rem}
p{margin:8px 0}.formula{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;background:#eef4ff;border:1px solid #d7e5ff;border-radius:12px;padding:12px;margin:10px 0;font-weight:750;color:var(--navy)}
.pill{background:#fff;border:1px solid #c8d9f4;border-radius:8px;padding:5px 9px}
.uses{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:9px;margin-top:10px}
.use{background:#f7f9fd;border-radius:11px;padding:10px 12px;font-size:.92rem}
.use b{color:var(--navy)}
.note{border-left:4px solid var(--red);padding:9px 12px;background:#fff6f5;border-radius:0 10px 10px 0;font-size:.92rem;margin-top:12px}
.mini{color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem}
.section-head{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin:28px 2px 12px}
.section-head h2{margin:0}.count{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);font-weight:700;background:#e9eef6;padding:5px 10px;border-radius:99px}
.exercise{margin-bottom:14px}
.instructions{color:var(--muted);margin-top:-3px;margin-bottom:14px}
.questions{display:grid;gap:10px}
.q{display:grid;grid-template-columns:30px 1fr minmax(150px,260px);align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid #e8edf5;border-radius:12px;background:#fcfdff}
.num{width:27px;height:27px;border-radius:50%;background:#eaf1fc;color:var(--navy);display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:.82rem;font-weight:800}
.qtext{font-size:.96rem}.q input{width:100%;min-width:0;border:1.5px solid #ccd7e6;border-radius:9px;padding:10px 11px;font:inherit;font-size:.94rem;outline:none;background:white}
.q input:focus{border-color:var(--blue);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px #0755b81a}
.q.correct{border-color:#9bd8b9;background:#f2fbf6}.q.incorrect{border-color:#efb4ae;background:#fff7f6}
.feedback{font-size:.8rem;margin-top:3px;min-height:1.1em;color:var(--muted)}
.actions{display:flex;gap:9px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:15px}
button{border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 16px;font:inherit;font-weight:750;cursor:pointer;transition:.15s}
.primary{background:var(--blue);color:white}.primary:hover{background:#064493;transform:translateY(-1px)}
.secondary{background:#edf2f8;color:#243750}.secondary:hover{background:#e0e8f2}
.result{font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);margin-left:auto}
.scorebar{height:8px;background:#e9eef5;border-radius:99px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:10px}.scorebar span{display:block;height:100%;width:0;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#0c8a58,#55c58b);transition:width .35s}
.footer{text-align:center;color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;padding:24px 10px 0}
.tip{font-size:.9rem;background:#f2f6fc;border-radius:12px;padding:12px;margin-top:12px}
@media(max-width:700px){.intro{grid-template-columns:1fr}.q{grid-template-columns:28px 1fr}.q input{grid-column:2}.uses{grid-template-columns:1fr}.result{margin-left:0;width:100%}.panel,.exercise{padding:16px}}
@media print{body{background:white}.hero{padding:15px}.logo{width:65px;height:65px}main{padding:10px}.exercise,.panel{box-shadow:none;break-inside:avoid}button{display:none}}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header class="hero">
  <img class="logo" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Castle School logo">
  <div class="brand">Castle School · English practice</div>
  <h1>The Present Perfect</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Understand it. Practise it. Master it.</p>
  <span class="level">B1 FOR SCHOOLS</span>
</header>
<main>
  <section class="intro">
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>1. How do we form it?</h2>
      <p>We use the <b>present perfect</b> to connect the past with the present. It is formed with <b>have / has + the past participle</b>.</p>
      <div class="formula"><span class="pill">I / You / We / They</span> have <span class="pill">finished</span></div>
      <div class="formula"><span class="pill">He / She / It</span> has <span class="pill">finished</span></div>
      <p><b>Past participle:</b> regular verbs usually end in <i>-ed</i> (played, watched). Irregular verbs have a special form (gone, seen, written).</p>
      <div class="note"><b>Remember!</b> Use <i>has</i> with he, she and it. Use <i>have</i> with I, you, we and they.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>2. Negative & questions</h2>
      <p><b>Negative:</b> subject + haven't / hasn't + past participle.</p>
      <div class="formula"><span class="pill">She</span> hasn't <span class="pill">finished</span>.</div>
      <p><b>Question:</b> Have / Has + subject + past participle?</p>
      <div class="formula"><span class="pill">Have</span> you <span class="pill">finished</span>?</div>
      <p><b>Short answers:</b> Yes, I have. / No, I haven't. · Yes, she has. / No, she hasn't.</p>
      <div class="tip">⚠️ Do not use <i>did</i> or the past simple form after have / has: <b>Have you seen</b> it? (NOT Have you saw it?)</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>3. When do we use it?</h2>
    <div class="uses">
      <div class="use"><b>Life experiences</b><br>At any time in your life; the exact time is not important.<br><i>I've visited London.</i></div>
      <div class="use"><b>Recent events</b><br>Something has happened recently and matters now.<br><i>She's just arrived.</i></div>
      <div class="use"><b>Unfinished time</b><br>A period that continues up to now.<br><i>We've had two tests this week.</i></div>
      <div class="use"><b>How long?</b><br>With <i>for</i> (a period) and <i>since</i> (a starting point).<br><i>I've lived here for a year.</i></div>
    </div>
    <p class="mini"><b>Common time words:</b> ever, never, just, already, yet, for, since. <i>Yet</i> usually comes at the end of questions and negative sentences.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Present perfect or past simple?</b> Use the past simple when the time is finished or stated: <i>I visited London last year.</i> Use the present perfect when the time is not stated or the period continues: <i>I've visited London twice.</i></div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>4. Let's practise!</h2><span class="count">40 QUESTIONS · INSTANT FEEDBACK</span></div>
  <section class="exercise" id="ex1">
    <h3>Exercise A · Affirmative sentences</h3>
    <p class="instructions">Complete each sentence with the correct present perfect form of the verb in brackets. Write the missing words.</p>
    <div class="questions" id="affirmative"></div>
    <div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="check('affirmative')">Check answers</button><button class="secondary" onclick="showAnswers('affirmative')">Show answers</button><button class="secondary" onclick="resetExercise('affirmative')">Try again</button><span class="result" id="result-affirmative"></span></div><div class="scorebar"><span id="bar-affirmative"></span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="exercise" id="ex2">
    <h3>Exercise B · Negative sentences</h3>
    <p class="instructions">Complete each sentence using haven't or hasn't + the past participle.</p>
    <div class="questions" id="negative"></div>
    <div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="check('negative')">Check answers</button><button class="secondary" onclick="showAnswers('negative')">Show answers</button><button class="secondary" onclick="resetExercise('negative')">Try again</button><span class="result" id="result-negative"></span></div><div class="scorebar"><span id="bar-negative"></span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="exercise" id="ex3">
    <h3>Exercise C · Questions</h3>
    <p class="instructions">Put the words in the correct order to make present perfect questions. Use the complete question, including the question mark.</p>
    <div class="questions" id="questions"></div>
    <div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="check('questions')">Check answers</button><button class="secondary" onclick="showAnswers('questions')">Show answers</button><button class="secondary" onclick="resetExercise('questions')">Try again</button><span class="result" id="result-questions"></span></div><div class="scorebar"><span id="bar-questions"></span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="exercise" id="ex4">
    <h3>Exercise D · Irregular verb challenge</h3>
    <p class="instructions">Write the past participle of each irregular verb. Spelling matters!</p>
    <div class="questions" id="irregular"></div>
    <div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="check('irregular')">Check answers</button><button class="secondary" onclick="showAnswers('irregular')">Show answers</button><button class="secondary" onclick="resetExercise('irregular')">Try again</button><span class="result" id="result-irregular"></span></div><div class="scorebar"><span id="bar-irregular"></span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="panel" style="margin-top:22px">
    <h2>🏆 Your practice score</h2>
    <p id="totalScore">Complete the exercises and check your answers to see your total score.</p>
    <div class="scorebar"><span id="totalBar"></span></div>
    <p class="mini">There are 40 questions in total. You can check your answers as many times as you like.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="footer">Castle School · B1 for Schools · Keep practising and you will improve!</div>
</main>
<script>
const data = {
affirmative: [
 {q:"I __________ (finish) my homework.",a:"have finished"},
 {q:"Mia __________ (visit) her grandparents this week.",a:"has visited"},
 {q:"We __________ (see) that film three times.",a:"have seen"},
 {q:"My friends __________ (buy) new trainers.",a:"have bought"},
 {q:"Tom __________ (do) his English project.",a:"has done"},
 {q:"You __________ (make) a lot of progress.",a:"have made"},
 {q:"The dog __________ (eat) all its food.",a:"has eaten"},
 {q:"I __________ (write) three emails today.",a:"have written"},
 {q:"Our teacher __________ (give) us some homework.",a:"has given"},
 {q:"They __________ (go) to the sports centre.",a:"have gone"}
],
negative: [
 {q:"I __________ (not / read) this book yet.",a:"haven't read"},
 {q:"Ella __________ (not / arrive) yet.",a:"hasn't arrived"},
 {q:"We __________ (not / do) the exercise.",a:"haven't done"},
 {q:"My brother __________ (not / clean) his room.",a:"hasn't cleaned"},
 {q:"They __________ (not / see) the new teacher.",a:"haven't seen"},
 {q:"Dad __________ (not / make) dinner yet.",a:"hasn't made"},
 {q:"You __________ (not / send) the message.",a:"haven't sent"},
 {q:"The bus __________ (not / come) yet.",a:"hasn't come"},
 {q:"I __________ (not / be) to Scotland.",a:"haven't been"},
 {q:"Lucy and Ben __________ (not / choose) a team.",a:"haven't chosen"}
],
questions: [
 {q:"you / ever / ride / a horse",a:"Have you ever ridden a horse?"},
 {q:"she / finish / her project / yet",a:"Has she finished her project yet?"},
 {q:"they / visit / the Science Museum",a:"Have they visited the Science Museum?"},
 {q:"your parents / see / this photo",a:"Have your parents seen this photo?"},
 {q:"he / ever / eat / sushi",a:"Has he ever eaten sushi?"},
 {q:"you / do / your homework",a:"Have you done your homework?"},
 {q:"the film / start / yet",a:"Has the film started yet?"},
 {q:"your friends / arrive",a:"Have your friends arrived?"},
 {q:"Mia / write / the email",a:"Has Mia written the email?"},
 {q:"how long / you / live / here",a:"How long have you lived here?"}
],
irregular: [
 {q:"go →",a:"gone"},{q:"see →",a:"seen"},{q:"write →",a:"written"},{q:"eat →",a:"eaten"},{q:"take →",a:"taken"},
 {q:"choose →",a:"chosen"},{q:"break →",a:"broken"},{q:"speak →",a:"spoken"},{q:"give →",a:"given"},{q:"know →",a:"known"}
]
};
const labels={affirmative:"Affirmative",negative:"Negative",questions:"Questions",irregular:"Irregular verbs"};
function render(){
 Object.keys(data).forEach(id=>{
  const host=document.getElementById(id);
  host.innerHTML=data[id].map((item,i)=>`<div class="q" id="${id}-q-${i}"><span class="num">${i+1}</span><div><div class="qtext">${item.q}</div><div class="feedback" id="${id}-f-${i}"></div></div><input type="text" id="${id}-a-${i}" aria-label="${labels[id]} answer ${i+1}" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="${id==='questions'?'Write the full question…':'Your answer…'}" onkeydown="if(event.key==='Enter')check('${id}')"></div>`).join('');
 });
}
function norm(s){return s.toLowerCase().trim().replace(/[’‘]/g,"'").replace(/[.!?]+$/g,"").replace(/\s+/g,"").replace(/'/g,"");}
function check(id){
 let score=0;
 data[id].forEach((item,i)=>{
  const input=document.getElementById(`${id}-a-${i}`), row=document.getElementById(`${id}-q-${i}`), fb=document.getElementById(`${id}-f-${i}`);
  const ok=norm(input.value)===norm(item.a);
  row.classList.toggle('correct',ok);row.classList.toggle('incorrect',!ok);
  fb.textContent=ok?"✓ Correct!":(input.value.trim()?`✗ Correct answer: ${item.a}`:"Type an answer. Correct answer: "+item.a);
  fb.style.color=ok?"#168451":"#b43c32";
  if(ok)score++;
 });
 document.getElementById(`result-${id}`).textContent=`${score} / 10`;
 document.getElementById(`bar-${id}`).style.width=(score*10)+"%";
 updateTotal();
}
function showAnswers(id){
 data[id].forEach((item,i)=>{document.getElementById(`${id}-a-${i}`).value=item.a;});
 check(id);
}
function resetExercise(id){
 data[id].forEach((item,i)=>{
  document.getElementById(`${id}-a-${i}`).value="";
  document.getElementById(`${id}-q-${i}`).classList.remove('correct','incorrect');
  document.getElementById(`${id}-f-${i}`).textContent="";
 });
 document.getElementById(`result-${id}`).textContent="";
 document.getElementById(`bar-${id}`).style.width="0%";
 updateTotal();
}
function updateTotal(){
 let total=0,checked=0;
 Object.keys(data).forEach(id=>{
  const result=document.getElementById(`result-${id}`).textContent;
  if(result){total+=parseInt(result,10);checked++;}
 });
 const el=document.getElementById("totalScore");
 if(!checked){el.textContent="Complete the exercises and check your answers to see your total score.";document.getElementById("totalBar").style.width="0%";return;}
 el.textContent=`Your checked score: ${total} / ${checked*10} (${Math.round(total/(checked*10)*100)}%). ${checked===4?(total>=36?"Excellent work! You're mastering the present perfect.":total>=28?"Good work! Review your mistakes and try again.":"Keep going! Practise the grammar notes and have another go."):"Keep going — check all four exercises for your score out of 40."}`;
 document.getElementById("totalBar").style.width=(total/40*100)+"%";
}
render();
</script>
</body>
</html>
